# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [3.4.2] - 2026-07-24

### Security
- **Comprehensive codebase hardening**
  - Add path traversal and URL validation for custom plugins (HTTPS-only, reject localhost/private IPs/embedded credentials)
  - Pin all external plugin/theme repos to specific release tags with shallow clones
  - Replace predictable temp directory with `mktemp -d` + restrictive permissions
  - Set `0o600` permissions on backup files and state files
  - Add binary/package name validators before shell interpolation
  - Sanitize theme/plugin names before writing to `.zshrc`
  - Harden self-update: verify git remote origin, use `--ignore-scripts` for npm
  - Add download sanity checks (shebang validation, file size bounds) in setup.sh
  - Remove dead code (`serviceManager.js`) with unsafe shell patterns

### Changed
- Track `package-lock.json` in version control for reproducible installs
- README: Add `brew trust` step to Homebrew installation instructions

## [3.4.0] - 2026-07-24

### Added
- **Update Notification** - Interactive self-update prompt on startup
  - Checks GitHub for newer versions (throttled: once per 24 hours)
  - Presents "Yes, update now / No / Skip this version" choices
  - Auto-detects install method (git pull or brew upgrade)
  - "Skip this version" prevents repeated prompts for same release
  - 5-second timeout, graceful degradation on network failure
- **ASCII art banner with version** in the Node.js CLI startup

### Changed
- Removed redundant version/feature text from setup.sh (Node.js CLI now handles the banner)

## [3.3.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Resume Setup** - Checkpoint-based state persistence for interrupted setups
  - Automatically saves progress at each major step (plugin selection, plugin installation, service installation, theme selection)
  - Detects incomplete state on re-launch and offers "Resume previous setup" or "Start fresh"
  - Resumes from exact point of interruption — only installs remaining plugins/services
  - Per-plugin progress tracking during installation (never re-installs what already succeeded)
  - 24-hour staleness expiry — expired state files are auto-discarded
  - Schema-versioned state file at `~/.awesome-lazy-zsh-state.json`
  - Graceful degradation — state I/O failures never crash the setup flow
  - Ctrl+C on resume prompt exits without modifying saved state
- **New module**: `stateManager` — state file read/write/validate/expire utilities

## [3.2.1] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Expanded Tool Installation** - 11 new installable tools:
  - Cloud CLI: AWS CLI, Google Cloud SDK, Azure CLI
  - DevOps: kubectl, Terraform, Ansible, Docker Compose
  - Languages: Python 3, Go, Rust, Java (OpenJDK)
- CLI tools and languages correctly skip the "Start services?" prompt

## [3.2.0] - 2026-07-22

### Added
- **Service Installation** - Actual server installation when selecting service plugins
  - Interactive prompt after plugin selection to install real servers
  - Granular multi-select for choosing which services to install
  - Platform auto-detection (Homebrew on macOS, apt/yum on Linux)
  - Pre-installation binary checks (skip already-installed services)
  - Post-install option to start services immediately
  - Progress reporting with final summary
  - Fail-forward strategy (one failure doesn't block others)
- **New modules**: serviceRegistry, platformDetector, serviceInstaller, serviceInstallFlow
- **Property-based tests** - 22 tests covering all correctness properties using fast-check
- **Test infrastructure** - Node.js built-in test runner with fast-check for PBT

### Supported Services (macOS/Linux)
- MongoDB Community Server (`brew tap mongodb/brew && brew install mongodb-community`)
- MySQL Community Server (`brew install mysql`)
- PostgreSQL (`brew install postgresql@14`)
- Redis (`brew install redis`)
- RabbitMQ (`brew install rabbitmq`)
- Elasticsearch (`brew tap elastic/tap && brew install elastic/tap/elasticsearch-full`)
- Memcached (`brew install memcached`)

## [3.1.8] - 2026-07-22

### Fixed
- **Spaceship Theme Symlink** - Create symlink even when theme directory already exists from prior install

## [3.1.7] - 2026-07-22

### Fixed
- **Oh My Zsh Plugin Loading** - Alias-only plugins (mongodb, mysql, redis, directories, history-search) no longer added to `plugins=()` array
- **Spaceship Theme** - Symlink created for Oh My Zsh to discover the theme
- Introduced `alias-only` marker in config.js to distinguish custom alias files from real Oh My Zsh plugins

## [3.1.6] - 2026-07-22

### Fixed
- **Homebrew Checksum Verification** - `get_homebrew_checksum` log_warning output no longer contaminates return value via command substitution
- Redirected warnings to stderr so `secure_download` correctly receives "skip" and bypasses verification

## [3.1.5] - 2026-01-09

